# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Virtual environments (never commit these)
venv/
.venv/
# Anchored to the repo root. An unanchored env/ matches at ANY depth, which
# silently swallowed sdi-intelligence-backend/env/ — configuration, not a
# virtualenv — and a file that cannot be committed is a file nobody can deploy.
/env/
.env
!config/*.example.env

# ── Output data (VERY IMPORTANT) ─────────────────────────────────────────
output/
*.json
*.jsonl
*.log
*.txt

# ── Input data (drawings, spreadsheets) ──────────────────────────────────
input/

# PDFs, images and workbooks (CRITICAL — job data, never commit)
*.pdf
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.xls
*.xlsx

# ── Backups / scratch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.bak
*.bak_*
*.backup
*~

# SQL dumps (schema lives in versioned .sql under sql/ if needed)
*.sql

# ── OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Explicit keeps (override the broad ignores above) ────────────────────
# A BROAD IGNORE PLUS ONE EXCEPTION IS A TRAP FOR THE NEXT FILE. `*.txt` above
# means every new .txt is invisible to `git add -A`, which reports nothing —
# requirements-dev.txt was written, committed, pushed and merged before anybody
# noticed it had never left the machine it was created on. Anything meant to be
# kept has to be named here.
!requirements.txt
!requirements-dev.txt
# CLIENT QUOTATION DATA IS NOT SOURCE CODE.
# This line used to read "!corpus/*.jsonl" -- an explicit exception that put the client
# corpora BACK after the *.jsonl rule above had excluded them. With src/corpus.jsonl that
# was 104,386 quotation records in the repository: customer names, job numbers, sell
# prices, cost breakdowns, rebate fractions, derived overhead divisors, and the names of
# the 39 estimators who prepared them, spanning 2006-2036 and 488 customers.
#
# Nothing reads them at estimate time. They are an INTERMEDIATE ARTEFACT: corpus_ingest.py
# writes one from the K: spreadsheets, and ingest_historical_to_db.py / _to_qdrant.py read
# it once to load SQL Server and the vector store. Both take the path as an argument and
# default to a RELATIVE corpus.jsonl, not to anything committed here. The engine's
# corpus-derived numbers are constants in config.py, with the corpus named in a comment as
# their provenance -- the file itself is not consulted.
#
# So it bought nothing and put SDI's own margin structure, and its clients' pricing
# history, on an external code host. The exception is removed and the ignore above stands.
corpus/
cache/
.sdi-commit
